 Step 1: Download MongoDB
Go to the official website:
MongoDB Community Server
Select:


Version → Latest


Platform → Windows


Package → MSI


Click Download.

🔷 Step 2: Install MongoDB


Open downloaded .msi file


Click Next


Accept License Agreement


Choose Complete Installation


Tick:


✅ Install MongoDB as a Service


✅ Install MongoDB Compass




Click Install


Finish setup



🔷 Step 3: Verify Installation
Open Command Prompt and type:
mongosh
If installation is successful:
test>
will appear.

🔷 Step 4: Create Database
In mongosh:
use collegeDB
Output:
switched to db collegeDB

🔷 Step 5: Check Database
show dbs
Database appears only after inserting data.

🔷 Step 6: Create Collection
db.createCollection("students")

🔷 Step 7: Show Collections
show collections
Output:
students

🔷 Step 8: Insert Document
6
👉 Insert One Document
db.students.insertOne({   name: "Apurv",   age: 21,   course: "AIDS"})
Output:
acknowledged: true

🔷 Step 9: View Documents
db.students.find()

🔷 Step 10: Insert Multiple Documents
db.students.insertMany([   {name:"Rahul", age:20, course:"CS"},   {name:"Sneha", age:22, course:"IT"}])

🔷 Step 11: Query Documents
👉 Find All
db.students.find()
👉 Find Specific
db.students.find({age:21})
👉 Pretty Format
db.students.find().pretty()

🔷 Step 12: Update Document
5
👉 Update One Document
db.students.updateOne(   {name:"Apurv"},   {$set:{age:22}})

🔷 Step 13: Delete Document
👉 Delete One Document
db.students.deleteOne({name:"Rahul"})

🔷 Step 14: Delete Multiple Documents
db.students.deleteMany({age:{$lt:22}})

🔷 Step 15: Drop Collection
db.students.drop()

🔷 Step 16: Drop Database
db.dropDatabase()

🔷 Step 17: Exit mongosh
exit

